    {
      "title": "Typography Personality",
      "content": "The system pairs three faces: Verlag (geometric grotesque) for UI and body, Verlag Condensed (compressed sans) for hero display, and Chronicle Text G1 (transitional serif) for occasional editorial accents. The wide-tracked all-caps label is the most recognizable typographic signature — 9–10px with 0.083–0.167em tracking reads as magazine sidebar text, not interface chrome. Body copy is unadorned 14–16px Verlag 400 with generous line-height; the voice is unhurried."
